# Dev Watchers — Prevent EMFILE (too many open files)

Next.js dev uses **Watchpack** (webpack). Without guardrails it watches parent folders (e.g. `~/apps/eduslide` with dozens of sibling apps), follows **`.cursor/rules` symlinks** to `~/apps/cursor/rules`, and exhausts file descriptors → `EMFILE`.

**Apply on every new app scaffold** — before first `./start.sh`.

## 1. Tailwind v4 — scoped scan only (`globals.css`)

```css
@import "tailwindcss" source(none);
@source "../**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}";
```

| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| ✅ `source(none)` on `@import "tailwindcss"` | Disables auto-scan of project root |
| ✅ `@source` paths stay under `src/` only | Never `@source "../../**"` or bare `@import "tailwindcss"` |
| ❌ Bare `@import "tailwindcss"` | Scans repo root + may follow `.cursor/rules` symlinks |

`globals.css` lives in `src/app/` — `../**` = `src/**` only.

## 2. `next.config.ts` — mandatory dev `watchOptions`

Copy this block into **every** new VTC Next.js app (adjust only if the app already has a custom `webpack` hook — merge, do not replace):

```typescript
import type { NextConfig } from 'next'
import path from 'path'

const projectRoot = path.resolve(__dirname)

const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  output: 'standalone',
  outputFileTracingRoot: projectRoot,
  turbopack: {},
  webpack: (config, { dev }) => {
    if (dev) {
      config.watchOptions = {
        ...config.watchOptions,
        followSymlinks: false,
        poll: 1000,
        aggregateTimeout: 300,
        ignored: [
          '**/node_modules/**',
          '**/.git/**',
          '**/.next/**',
          '**/.cursor/**',
          // App inside a suite folder (eduslide/eduassign, crm_suite/…)
          path.join(projectRoot, '..', '**'),
        ],
      }
    }
    return config
  },
}

export default nextConfig
```

| Option | Why |
|--------|-----|
| `followSymlinks: false` | Do not traverse `.cursor/rules` → `~/apps/cursor/rules` |
| `path.join(projectRoot, '..', '**')` | Ignore sibling apps in suite / `~/apps` |
| `poll: 1000` | Safer on WSL / low `ulimit` (optional but recommended) |

**Strings only** in `ignored` — Next.js webpack schema rejects function callbacks.

### Next.js 16+ production build (Docker)

The `webpack` hook above is **dev-only** (`if (dev)`). Next.js 16 defaults `next build` to **Turbopack**; a `webpack` key without `turbopack` fails the platform Docker build.

| Required | Why |
|----------|-----|
| `turbopack: {}` in `next.config` | Silences the Turbopack/webpack clash — reference: `~/apps/jobs/next.config.ts` |
| `"build": "next build --webpack"` in `package.json` | Belt-and-suspenders for Docker (`npm run build` on build.vtc.com) |

Run `npm run build` locally before push — same command as the platform image build (`deployment.mdc`).

## 3. Cursor rules — copy, do not symlink

```bash
~/cursor_rules/scripts/push-stub.sh ~/apps/my-app
# Creates/refreshes: my-app/.cursor/rules/00-vtc-central.mdc
# Agents read ~/cursor_rules/rules/ from that stub.
```

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Install the stub via `add.sh` / `new.sh` / `push-stub.sh` | Symlink `.cursor/rules` → `~/cursor_rules/rules` (webpack EMFILE) |
| Gitignore `.cursor/` | Commit `.cursor/` |
| Edit rules in `~/cursor_rules/rules/` | Copy the rule pack into the app |

## 4. Workspace and suite folders

| Situation | Do |
|-----------|-----|
| Developing one app | Open Cursor workspace at **`~/apps/my-app`** or **`~/apps/eduslide/eduassign`**, not the suite parent |
| Eduslide placeholders | Do **not** link `.cursor/rules` until the app has a real scaffold (`package.json`). Run `link-cursor.sh` when building that app |
| Suite root (`eduslide/`) | Catalogue only — no `.cursor/rules` on the parent |

## 5. `start.sh` — mandatory EMFILE guard (Linux / WSL)

Every app **`start.sh`** must set polling and raise `ulimit` before `npm run dev`:

```bash
# Avoid EMFILE: native watchers climb parent dirs / .cursor/rules symlinks on Linux & WSL.
if ulimit -n 65536 2>/dev/null; then
  :
else
  ulimit -n 8192 2>/dev/null || true
fi
export WATCHPACK_POLLING=true
export WATCHPACK_POLLING_INTERVAL=1000
export CHOKIDAR_USEPOLLING=true
```

Use **`./start.sh`** for local dev — do not run bare `npm run dev` on Linux/WSL unless you export the vars above manually.

| Variable | Why |
|----------|-----|
| `ulimit -n 65536` | Raises open-file ceiling (fallback `8192`) |
| `WATCHPACK_POLLING=true` | Webpack uses polling instead of native `inotify` |
| `WATCHPACK_POLLING_INTERVAL=1000` | Poll interval ms |
| `CHOKIDAR_USEPOLLING=true` | Next/Turbopack chokidar companion |

Reference: `~/apps/chat/start.sh`, `~/apps/jwt/start.sh`, builder template `start.sh`.

